Subject: [PATCH] qemuarm64: store the boot environment on the FAT partition

Use the first virtio disk's FAT partition for the persistent boot environment
and enable the commands used by the Leda boot scripts.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Leda-specific boot environment]

diff --git a/configs/qemu_arm64_defconfig b/configs/qemu_arm64_defconfig
--- a/configs/qemu_arm64_defconfig
+++ b/configs/qemu_arm64_defconfig
@@ -38,7 +38,12 @@ CONFIG_CMD_EFIDEBUG=y
 CONFIG_CMD_TPM=y
 CONFIG_CMD_MTDPARTS=y
 CONFIG_CMD_SPAWN=y
-CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_FLASH=y
+CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_FAT=y
+CONFIG_ENV_FAT_INTERFACE="virtio"
+CONFIG_ENV_FAT_DEVICE_AND_PART="0:1"
+CONFIG_CMD_NVEDIT_LOAD=y
+CONFIG_CMD_FAT=y
+CONFIG_CMD_BOOTMENU=y
 CONFIG_SCSI_AHCI=y
 CONFIG_AHCI_PCI=y
 CONFIG_DFU_TFTP=y
